    <string name="feature_settings_about_text">A local music player. Free, no ads, no account. Made in Brazil, with AI assistance under the author’s direction and review.</string>
    <string name="feature_settings_privacy_text">Your library, your settings, your profile (name, photo, cover, description) and your listening stats stay on your device only. The app has no account, no ads and sends nothing about you anywhere.\n\nWhen you open an artist, or see your artists on Home and in the Library, the app asks Deezer for public information about them (photo, popular songs, discography) using only the artist’s name; if Deezer doesn’t know them, it asks MusicBrainz and the Cover Art Archive instead. For the biography, it asks Last.fm (through our own server, which only adds the access key) using the artist’s name. Searching for artists in the Library sends what you type to Deezer. For the artists you follow, the app checks Deezer for new releases about twice a day, using only their Deezer pages.\n\nLyrics are looked up on LRCLIB only when you open them (or pick them for the share banner), using the song title, artist, album and length. Sharing a song sends a YouTube Music search link for it; nothing is looked up online. Fixing tags automatically asks Deezer (or, if it finds nothing, MusicBrainz and the Cover Art Archive) and Last.fm using the song’s title, artist and length, only when you tap Search. When you open the app, it asks GitHub whether there is a new version.\n\nWith offline mode on (Settings → System), the app doesn’t go online at all, except to check for updates.\n\nThe app asks for music and audio, to read the songs on your phone, and, on Android 13 and newer, for notifications, only for release alerts. When you save tags, Android asks you to allow changing that file. The app doesn’t ask for photos, videos, contacts or location.</string>
